    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): On its own, [ev-0a3ad54fc240] is just a list item, but it sits in the \"Metrics namespace\" section. [ev-1f419676f177] says what the change is. Metrics that started with the `cortex_` prefix will now start with `loki_`, so `cortex_query_scheduler_inflight_requests` is renamed to `loki_query_scheduler_inflight_requests` (subject: the metric name; change: prefix rename). [ev-1f419676f177] also says who is exposed: setups that keep the default `metrics_namespace` value `loki`, since changing it to `cortex` keeps the old prefix. It also notes that this setting is deprecated and will be removed. The consequence is that the metric is no longer published under its old `cortex_` name, so anything that looks it up by that name stops finding it. An engineer can write the typed assertion from this.",
